  "acceptance_criteria": [
    "The project must run locally using `python -m http.server`.",
    "Users must be able to import industrial input bundles via FileReader or textarea.",
    "The app must process imported data and display scored highlights sorted by score in descending order.",
    "Filter controls must be visible and functional for fields like streamer, game, category, and score.",
    "Users must be able to manually tag highlights and append new items to the dataset.",
    "Export functionality must generate downloadable files using Blob and URL.createObjectURL.",
    "Domain fields such as streamer, game, timestamp, category, intensity, chatRate, keywords, title, description, and score must be used.",
    "The project runs as a local static browser app from index.html.",
    "The GUI imports both sample JSON arrays and full industrial input bundle objects.",
    "The app scores, sorts, filters, manually appends, persists, and exports highlight candidates using implemented modules.",
    "Browser smoke tests and industrial I/O smoke tests validate the real generated UI."
  ]
